# The menu program's data: name, address, C declaration (%s is the name), what it is.  scripts/gen_menu_symbols.py writes
# native/menu_symbols.h (the declarations) and native/menu.ld (the names at their addresses), so the C names no address.
work_area         0x00000caa  uint32_t *%s    pointer to a buffer of 80 longs that clear_work_area clears
shadow_table      0x00000e10  uint16_t %s[]   a table of words indexed by shadow_set / shadow_get (colour register shadows)
mouse_x           0x0001e4fc  uint16_t %s     pointer position, 0 to $200 (moved by input_poll)
mouse_y           0x0001e4fe  uint16_t %s     pointer position, 0 to $C7
mouse_x_copy      0x0001e500  uint16_t %s
mouse_y_copy      0x0001e502  uint16_t %s
button_bits       0x0001e504  uint8_t %s[2]   bit 0: a button down (either), bit 1: the second; cleared at the start of every poll
mouse_counter     0x0001e506  uint16_t %s     JOY0DAT as last read: vertical counter in the high byte, horizontal in the low byte
mouse_counter_old 0x0001e508  uint16_t %s     the value before it
button_presses    0x0001e50a  uint8_t %s      bits set by input_poll (1 first button, 4 second or the pot lines), cleared by whoever reads them
pending_request   0x0001e5a8  uint32_t %s     non-zero: something is waiting to be taken (take_pending_request)
joystick          0x0001e5ac  uint8_t %s      bit 0 up, 1 down, 2 left, 3 right, 7 fire
